                    "max": 0,
                    "message": {
                      "_ref": "68f6016896499",
                      "content": "Rules:  \n1. The plan must always be reasonable given the information currently available.  \n2. If the mission can be completed directly and safely, plan the full set of steps.  \n3. If the mission is too broad or lacks information, reduce the scope to a smaller set of safe, useful steps (\u201cscope down\u201d).  \n4. Never mix action types: a plan must be entirely exploratory, entirely executive, or entirely a report.  \n5. Keep actions progressive: if the task is complex, plan safe incremental steps, then reassess after execution.  \n\nIllustrative examples (for understanding only, do not copy literally):  \n- If the mission is to address climate change, the plan should only identify key stakeholders or gather initial data, not solve the entire problem.  \n- If the mission is to build a rocket without any expertise, the plan should start with researching training or resources.  \n- If the mission is to contact someone, the plan should first check if it is possible and appropriate to do so.  ",
                      "contentType": "default",
